                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So I wasn't expecting much for $.49 and my very low expectations were met.  I played this on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers and there were no issues.  My main complaint is the button mapping or Touch configuration.  You have to press down on the joystick to initiate thrusters (always a bad choice) and worse than that, your hands are tilted the wrong way so that to thrust forward and up in the air, you have to contort your hands so that you're going the right direction. \n\nI must admit that it is fun to launch behind the backcourt and thrust up in the air all the way to dunk the basketball.  Michael Jordan dunking the ball from the free throw line seems rather pedestrian after this glorious stunt.  I imagine this is how basketball will be played in the future.  Somebody invent personal jetpacks ASAP!\n\nThe shooting is rather awful in this game.  Even shooting in the lobby in REC ROOM is better than in this game.  So this basketball game probably has the worst shooting mechanics of any game ever made.  The dribbling is almost as bad.  \n\nBut we're here to dunk.  You don't really need a roomscale setup.  You can spawn the ball to your hand (press B on the Touch controller).  Then just initiate thrusters in either hand or both for maximum effect.  But other than trying trick dunks and enjoying thrusting up in the air, there isn't much to do.  Luckily, it is fun to try trick dunks.  \n\nRate 5/10 Sale Price of $.49 deserves a 5 out of 10 (dev needs to fix the Touch configuration so that the difficulty isn't in the way the thrusters are aligned to make it a 6 or higher)",
